@startuml
title UC-02 - Configure Application Environment (Main Flow)

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Developer
boundary "Web UI" as UI
database "Browser\nsessionStorage" as DraftStore
control "Environment Configuration\nAPI / Controller" as API
control "Environment Configuration Service" as Service
entity "Application Query /\nApplication Repository" as AppRepo
control "Resource Output Catalog /\nResource Definition Query" as ResourceCatalog
control "Workload Output Catalog" as WorkloadCatalog
control "Environment Configuration Validator" as Validator
collections "Secret Store /\nSecret Management Adapter" as SecretStore
entity "Environment Configuration Repository" as ConfigRepo

note over UI, DraftStore
  EnvironmentConfigurationDraft is a CLIENT-OWNED DTO.
  sessionStorage contains only non-sensitive values and opaque
  references; plaintext Secret is never written there.
end note

note over API, SecretStore
  requestResourceOutputs(), requestWorkloadOutputs(),
  listValidOutputs(), listValidSensitiveOutputs(), and storeSecret()
  are internal query/integration messages, not UC system operations.
  Secret staging/cleanup remains governed by D07.
end note

Developer -> UI: Open application Configuration page
Developer -> UI: Select environment (staging or production)
UI -> API: selectEnvironment(applicationId, environment)
API -> Service: selectEnvironment(applicationId, environment)
Service -> AppRepo: loadConfigurationRequirements(applicationId)
AppRepo --> Service: Latest Application Definition version,\nworkloads, variables, secrets and dependencies
Service -> ConfigRepo: find(applicationId, environment)
ConfigRepo --> Service: Current configuration and opaque revision, or none
Service --> API: Requirements and configuration with\nbaseApplicationDefinitionVersion + baseConfigurationRevision
API --> UI: Display variables and secrets by workload
UI -> DraftStore: restore matching draft or\nsave initialized non-sensitive draft

loop For each Environment Variable
    Developer -> UI: Select value source
    alt Direct value
        Developer -> UI: Enter value
        UI -> UI: setDirectConfigurationValue(configurationDraft, variable, value)
    else Resource Output
        Developer -> UI: Select a resource that the workload depends on
        UI -> API: requestResourceOutputs(resource)
        API -> Service: requestResourceOutputs(resource)
        Service -> ResourceCatalog: listValidOutputs(resource)
        ResourceCatalog --> Service: Valid resource outputs
        Service --> API: Valid resource outputs
        API --> UI: Display valid resource outputs
        Developer -> UI: Select resource output
        UI -> UI: bindResourceOutput(configurationDraft, variable, resource, output)
    else Workload Output
        Developer -> UI: Select a workload that the workload depends on
        UI -> API: requestWorkloadOutputs(workload)
        API -> Service: requestWorkloadOutputs(workload)
        Service -> WorkloadCatalog: listValidOutputs(workload)
        WorkloadCatalog --> Service: Valid workload outputs
        Service --> API: Valid workload outputs
        API --> UI: Display valid workload outputs
        Developer -> UI: Select workload output
        UI -> UI: bindWorkloadOutput(configurationDraft, variable, workload, output)
    end
    UI -> DraftStore: save(nonSensitiveConfigurationDraft)
end

loop For each Secret
    Developer -> UI: Select secret source
    alt Enter a secret value securely
        Developer -> UI: Enter secret value
        UI -> API: setDirectConfigurationValue(secret, secretValue)
        API -> Service: setDirectConfigurationValue(secret, secretValue)
        Service -> SecretStore: storeSecret(applicationId, environment, secretValue)
        SecretStore --> Service: Opaque Secret reference
        Service --> API: Opaque Secret reference
        API --> UI: Replace plaintext with opaque reference
    else Sensitive Resource Output
        Developer -> UI: Select a depended-on resource\nand its sensitive output
        UI -> API: requestResourceOutputs(resource)
        API -> Service: requestResourceOutputs(resource)
        Service -> ResourceCatalog: listValidSensitiveOutputs(resource)
        ResourceCatalog --> Service: Valid sensitive outputs
        Service --> API: Valid sensitive outputs
        API --> UI: Display valid sensitive outputs
        Developer -> UI: Select sensitive output
        UI -> UI: bindResourceOutput(configurationDraft, secret, resource, output)
    end
    UI -> DraftStore: save(draft with opaque references only)
end

Developer -> UI: Select Save Configuration
UI -> API: saveEnvironmentConfiguration(completeDraft, bases)
API -> Service: saveEnvironmentConfiguration(completeDraft, bases)
Service -> AppRepo: findLatestVersion(applicationId)
AppRepo --> Service: Current latest Application Definition version
Service -> ConfigRepo: findRevision(applicationId, environment)
ConfigRepo --> Service: Current configuration revision or none
Service -> Validator: validateEnvironmentConfiguration(completeDraft)
Validator --> Service: Validation successful
Service -> ConfigRepo: saveIfBasesMatch(completeDraft, bases)
note right of ConfigRepo
  Both base comparisons and the durable write are one
  atomic transaction/CAS; two writers cannot both win.
end note

alt Repository returns DRAFT_CONFLICT
    ConfigRepo --> Service: DRAFT_CONFLICT (no write)
    Service --> API: DRAFT_CONFLICT (no write)
    API --> UI: Require reload and review/reapply\nkeep browser draft
    UI --> Developer: Show concurrent edit conflict
else Repository commits configuration
    ConfigRepo --> Service: Environment Configuration saved
    Service --> API: Configuration saved
    API --> UI: Show save confirmation
    UI -> DraftStore: remove(configurationDraft)
    UI --> Developer: Environment Configuration saved
end

@enduml
